course: dictionary
lesson: 9012
title: A slang word with a warning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are slang, which means informal words people use in everyday chat. «He'd had a skinful» is a slang phrase used in Britain and Australia. Read the clues: a skinful is a large amount, and here the amount is alcohol, the drink in beer, wine and spirits.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «He'd had a lot of alcohol» fits, so «skinful» means enough alcohol to make someone drunk. Slang like this is for grown-ups to understand, not for children to use.
explain: Alcohol is harmful, especially for children, because children's bodies are still growing. If you read or hear this word, the safe thing is to ask a grown-up what it means.
fact: Skinful is a noun, so you can say «a skinful» or «have a skinful».
fact: «Skinful» is slang, used mostly in Britain and Australia.
fact: «Skinful» means a large amount of alcohol, enough to make someone drunk.
fact: Alcohol is harmful, especially for children, so children must never drink it.
fact: In your own writing, use plain words such as «drunk» or «drank too much» instead of slang.
exercise: «He'd had a skinful.» What does skinful mean here? | *Enough alcohol to make him drunk | A new pair of shoes | A tiny drink of water | A long sleep
exercise: Where is «skinful» mostly used as slang? | *Britain and Australia | Only on the moon | Nowhere at all, because it is not a real word
exercise: Why must children never drink alcohol? | *It is harmful to children | It tastes of sweets | It makes children faster runners | It makes children taller
test: Which of these means the same as «had a skinful» in plain words? | Ate a very big lunch | Went swimming for hours | *Drank far too much alcohol
test: What is the best thing to do when you meet a slang word you do not know? | *Read the clues, then ask a grown-up or check a dictionary | Skip it and never think about it again | Make up a meaning and say it aloud
exam: Why is «skinful» a word for adults rather than children? | Because it means having a bath | Because it is a French word | Because it is too long to spell | *Because alcohol is harmful to children
